The only missing thing is added an unit test to cover from regressions

Triage-bot woke this up.  Is this IPVS-specific or does it affect other modes?

It seems wrong to me for an `eTP: Local` service to even try to use a pod that is not local.  Whether that should result in an ICMP response or not, I think is debatable.

@danwinship since nftables is set to replace iptables mode and may well obviate IPVS mode, is this something you want to weigh in on?

@haircommander I agree with you.

I have tested K8S 1.22.0/1.23.0/1.24.0/1.25.2 on ubuntu22-04(with cgroup v2) and ubuntu18-04(with cgroup v1). `K8S 1.22.0~1.25.2  on ubuntu18-04` and `K8S 1.22.0~1.23.0 on ubuntu22-04` work as my expect (can only access/modifying its own cgroup in privileged pod), but `K8S 1.24.0~1.25.2 on ubuntu22-04` is different.

Trun off cgroup v2 on ubuntu22-04 and use cgroup v1, K8S 1.25.2 works as my expect!

